APKBUILD changes for the armv7 debug build.

Apply by hand to community/freeunit/APKBUILD in your aports checkout
together with arm-alignment-debug.patch from this directory.

1) Add the patch to source=
---------------------------
source="$pkgname-$pkgver.tar.gz::https://github.com/freeunitorg/freeunit/archive/refs/tags/$pkgver.tar.gz
	$pkgname.initd
	$pkgname.confd
	$pkgname.logrotate
	phpver.patch
	fix-py-3-14.patch
	fix-py-upload-edge-cases.patch
	arm-alignment-debug.patch
	"

Then: cd community/freeunit && abuild checksum

2) UBSan alignment instrumentation in build()
---------------------------------------------
Insert the case-block BEFORE the first ./configure call:

build() {
	local _otel=--otel
	case "$CARCH" in
		arm*|ppc64le|x86) _otel='' ;;
	esac

	# armv7 SIGBUS hunt: UBSan + symbols.  Remove after fix lands.
	case "$CARCH" in
		armhf|armv7)
			export CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -fsanitize=alignment,undefined \
			              -fno-sanitize-recover=alignment \
			              -fno-omit-frame-pointer -g3 -O1"
			export LDFLAGS="$LDFLAGS -fsanitize=alignment,undefined"
			;;
	esac

	./configure \
		...

3) Make the crash observable during check()
-------------------------------------------
Temporarily flip these in check() so SIGBUS surfaces as a test
failure with the router stderr captured, instead of being silently
allowed and reaped:

	case "$CARCH" in
		armhf | armv7) _allow_fail=no ;;  # was: yes
	esac

	# Comment out for the debug run:
	# pkill -f 'unitd.*--no-daemon' 2>/dev/null || true

Revert both to current values once a fix is in.

4) Reproduce
------------
docker run --rm --privileged multiarch/qemu-user-static --reset -p yes
docker run --platform linux/arm/v7 -it --rm \
  -e APORTSDIR=/mnt -v $(pwd):/mnt \
  --ulimit nofile=65536:65536 \
  registry.alpinelinux.org/alpine/infra/docker/alpine-gitlab-ci:latest \
  sh -c "sleep infinity"
docker exec -it --user buildozer <id> ash
cd /mnt/community/freeunit
abuild checksum
abuild -r 2>&1 | tee /tmp/build.log

5) Read the output
------------------
UBSan diagnostics look like:
  src/nxt_http_parse.c:414:24: runtime error: load of misaligned
  address 0xaabbccdd for type 'uint64_t', which requires 8 byte
  alignment

SIGBUS handler lines look like:
  unit[armdbg]: SIGBUS si_addr=0x... pc=0x76abcdef ...

Resolve PCs against the built binary:
  addr2line -e src/freeunit-1.35.3/build/sbin/unitd -fC 0x76abcdef

Bisect markers ("unit[armdbg]: pre/post ...") narrow the trap to
either nxt_h1p_init or nxt_http_response_hash_init even when stderr
is truncated.

6) Suspect ranking (from source review)
---------------------------------------
- nxt_http_ver_t union @ src/nxt_http_parse.h:23-33
  (uint64_t aliased with u_char[8], no nxt_aligned(8))
- nxt_http_request_parse_t.version @ src/nxt_http_parse.h:49
  (no aligned attribute; .version after string structs)
- nxt_port_queue_t / nxt_nncq_t shm atomics
  (shm offset can be 4-aligned; see src/nxt_port_queue.h, nxt_nncq.h)
- nxt_thread_time_t 64-bit time_t / nxt_nsec_t

Fix template once a line is identified:
  typedef union {
      ...
  } nxt_aligned(8) nxt_http_ver_t;

or:
  uint64_t v __attribute__((aligned(8)));
  nxt_memcpy(&v, p, 8);
  if (v == http11_ui64 || ...)
